# Illusionary Mask's {X} paid with {U}{U}{U} from Black Lotus (the pool empty right after the activation, CR 601.2h): the mana
# spent on X decides what may be chosen, by amount and by type (the ruling) - Waterwind Scout's {2}{U} (3, exactly X), never
# Giant Octopus's {3}{U} (one more) nor Balduvian Bears' {1}{G} (no green spent), nor a matching card in the opponent's hand
# ("in your hand"). The Scout is cast face down as a 2/2 creature spell (CR 708.4), resolves face down (its "enters" ability
# never applies, CR 708.3), and on turn 3 its attack would tap it: instead it is turned face up and becomes tapped (CR 614.1,
# 701.26a), attacking as the flying 2/2 Scout, and turning up makes no Map token (CR 708.8).

[Bot1 Deck]
Illusionary Mask
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Waterwind Scout
Giant Octopus
Balduvian Bears
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Aegis Turtle
Island x24

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Illusionary Mask.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Illusionary Mask.Activate(X: 3)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Mana =
! Bot1.Choose(Giant Octopus)
! Bot1.Choose(Balduvian Bears)
! Bot1.Choose(Aegis Turtle)
Bot1.Choose(Waterwind Scout)
Bot1.Accept
? Stack..FaceDown = true
? Stack..FaceDownName = Waterwind Scout
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
? Bot1.Battlefield..Power = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield..Keywords = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(#1 > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Waterwind Scout.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Waterwind Scout.FaceDown = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Waterwind Scout.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Map Token = (absent)
